<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-VENTSPILS RELOADINGS SLIGHTLY LOWER IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-VENTSPILS RELOADINGS SLIGHTLY LOWER IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reloadings of crude oil and oil products at Latvia's Ventspils oil terminal in April came to 2.1 million tonnes, 400,000 tonnes lower than March, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The terminal, one of the main outlets for Russian crude in the region, said in a statement that it reloaded 1.2 million tonnes of crude oil while diesel reloadings came to 684,500.</p>
<p>Ventspils Bafta said that so far this year a total of 8.8 million tonnes of oil and oil products has been reloaded, some 400,000 tonnes more than during the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
